1. An independent set of size ⌈√n⌉, OR
2. A cycle of length at least ⌈√n⌉

This is a known graph theory problem. I'll use DFS to:
- Detect cycles when we see a back-edge to an ancestor that's far enough away
- If no long cycle exists, construct an independent set using BFS levels

